## Types

The back-index is one remote timer `Trigger` per bot in a space, whose input names everything a run needs.

```mdl
type BackIndexInput
  desc: The trigger's input; ConfigureBackIndex writes it and CrawlDiscordChannels reads it.
  fields:
    applicationId: string             # the Discord app (bot) installed in the server
    channels: string[]                # top-level Discord channel ids to crawl
    descendThreads?: boolean          # default true
    maxDays?: number                  # lookback for a channel crawled for the first time
    maxDepth?: number
    maxSteps?: number                 # pages one run reads; default 2
    state: Ref<CrawlState>
```

The bot host answers messages in Discord's own field names, trimmed to what the crawl maps; nothing else of the API
response crosses.

```mdl
type DiscordMessage
  fields:
    id: string
    type: number
    content: string
    timestamp: string
    author: { id: string, username: string, global_name?: string }
    mentions: { id: string, username: string, global_name?: string }[]
    referenced_message?: { id: string }
    message_reference?: { message_id: string }
    thread?: { id: string, name: string }
```

```mdl
type DiscordSourceChannel
  fields:
    id: string
    name: string
    guildId: string
    guildName: string
```

## Services

```mdl
service DiscordService
  desc: |
    The crawl's only dependency on Discord: the two source calls it reads through, and nothing else of the bot. The
    app reaches it over EDGE's `/discord/bots/:applicationId` routes, signed with the user's identity; a plugin bundle
    on EDGE reaches it through compute-service's invocation scope. Both end at the bot host, which signs the Discord
    call with the bot's token.
  ops:
    listChannels(bot: { applicationId: string, spaceId: string }) → DiscordSourceChannel[]
    fetchMessages(bot: { applicationId: string, spaceId: string }, channelId: string, after: string, limit: number) → DiscordMessage[]
  errors:
    DiscordBotError: the bot does not serve the space, is not running, or the channel is outside the servers the space connected
```

The crawl writes facts with `MemoryService.put` (`@dxos/echo-memory`), one call per extracted page, the same
service brain and agent memory write through; a repeated put is idempotent, so a page read again is harmless.

## Runtime

The trigger runs CrawlDiscordChannels on EDGE, where compute-service's `plugins` routing loads plugin-discord's
bundle as a Dynamic Worker through the worker loader. A bundle gets services only through its invocation scope, by
service key, so the crawl's services must each have a key there:

| Service            | How the bundle gets it                                                    |
|--------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `AiService`        | the bundle's `FUNCTIONS_AI_SERVICE` binding                               |
| `Database.Service` | the bundle's `DATA_SERVICE` binding                                       |
| `DiscordService`   | an invocation-scope key, dispatched to discord-service's agent entrypoint |
| `MemoryService`    | an invocation-scope key, dispatched to the space's memory on EDGE         |

## Operations

```mdl
op ConfigureBackIndex
  key: org.dxos.operation.discord.configureBackIndex
  desc: Creates or updates the space's back-index for a bot: its CrawlState and the remote timer trigger.
  input:
    applicationId: string
    channels: string[]
    trigger?: Ref<Trigger>        # the back-index to reconfigure; a new one when absent
    name?: string
    cron?: string                 # default every two minutes
    enabled?: boolean
  output: { trigger: Ref<Trigger>, state: Ref<CrawlState> }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
```

```mdl
op CrawlDiscordChannels
  key: org.dxos.operation.discord.crawlChannels
  desc: One bounded run of the back-index, as the trigger invokes it.
  services: [AiService, Database.Service, DiscordService, MemoryService]
  input: BackIndexInput
  output: { done: boolean, errored: number, steps: number, messages: number, error?: string }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write, memory:write, ai]
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Setup on the Discord connection's page

  req F-1.1: plugin-connector's connection page has a connector section, a surface each connector can fill for its own connections; plugin-discord fills it for the Discord sign-in connection, so setting up the space's back-index needs no agent.

  req F-1.2: The section lists the servers the connection's account manages, with installing the bot where it is missing and indexing it where it is installed. Indexing asks the bot host for an index grant (F-8); only then are the server's text and announcement channels listed, each with a toggle that adds it to or removes it from the back-index.

  req F-1.3: Each toggle applies at once: the first creates the back-index with ConfigureBackIndex, later ones update its channels in place, so a space has one back-index per bot. No channel is indexed until it is picked.

  req F-1.4: Removing the last channel, or no longer indexing the server, disables the trigger and keeps its CrawlState and the memory it filled.

  req F-1.5: Each indexed channel shows its crawl status (waiting, crawling, up to date, or the error), and the section shows the messages read, the last run, the history and interval settings, and Pause or Resume.

  req F-1.6: Setup asks for no token when the bot is Kai. The connection is the person's sign-in, which the grant check reads; a pasted bot token connection gets no section, since it cannot show who manages a server. The agent's Discord companion keeps routing channels to the agent and shows which are indexed, but does not index.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Pipeline

  req F-2.1: A run is DiscordPipeline's assembly, with the same stages as the Discord facts CLI: persist message, agent profile, extract questions, extract facts, topics, answer questions.

  req F-2.2: Only the stores differ from the CLI: the frontier and cursors live in the CrawlState ECHO object, facts are put into the space's memory with MemoryService.put, and Topics and Persons are written to the space.

  req F-2.3: The crawl writes no fact feed; MemoryService is the only place its facts go.

  req F-2.4: A run reads at most maxSteps pages and resumes from the CrawlState on the next trigger, so a message read again unchanged costs no model call.
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Reading as the bot
  uses: [DiscordService, DiscordMessage, DiscordSourceChannel]

  req F-3.1: The crawl's Discord source is built only on DiscordService.listChannels and fetchMessages, its one Discord dependency; no Discord API request, path or header crosses from a plugin to the bot host.

  req F-3.2: The bot host answers listChannels with the text and announcement channels of the servers the space was granted, and of its agents' servers while it owns the bot, and nothing for any other server the bot is in.

  req F-3.3: The bot host answers fetchMessages only for a channel or thread in one of those servers, with at most `limit` messages after `after`, oldest first.

  req F-3.4: The bot host refuses both calls for a space with no grant that does not own the bot; reads need no running gateway.

  req F-3.5: compute-service refuses a call whose bot names a space other than the invocation's own.
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Token custody

  req F-4.1: Kai's token never leaves the bot host: not to compute-service, not to a plugin bundle, not to the app, and not into the space.

  req F-4.2: The back-index names only the bot. The bot host signs every read with the token the bot runs on: Kai's, which EDGE holds, or, for a bot that is not Kai, the AccessToken the space gave when it connected the bot.

  req F-4.3: No answer of the bot host carries a token, an authorization header or a raw Discord API response.
```

```mdl
feat F-5: Failures

  req F-5.1: A run never fails its invocation: its error and outcome are written to the CrawlState, so they outlive the run.

  req F-5.2: A source call the bot host refuses marks the channel as errored in the CrawlState with the host's reason, and the run carries on with the other channels.
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Pipeline panel

  req F-6.1: Brain's Pipeline panel reads the back-index's state from its ECHO objects (the CrawlState and the trigger), not from a file the CLI wrote.
```

```mdl
feat F-8: Index grants

  req F-8.1: A space reads a server only under an index grant, which the bot host gives when a person who owns the server or holds Manage Server there asks, as their own Discord sign-in shows.

  req F-8.2: A grant is kept apart from agent bindings: granting or revoking never claims or releases the bot's owner, starts or stops its gateway, or changes how a message is routed.

  req F-8.3: Several spaces can hold grants for one bot, each reading only its own granted servers.

  req F-8.4: Revoking a grant, or deleting the space, removes it; the space's next read of that server is refused.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: Runtime

  req F-7.1: CrawlDiscordChannels runs on EDGE as plugin-discord's bundle in a Dynamic Worker loaded by compute-service's worker loader, not on operation-service.

  req F-7.2: compute-service's invocation scope offers DiscordService and MemoryService to the bundle by service key, each pinned to the invocation's space.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Index a channel with Kai
  given: a space with no agent and a Discord connection; Kai installed in the DXOS server; the person manages it
  when: on the Discord connection's page the person indexes the DXOS server and picks #general
  then:
    - one Trigger and CrawlState exist, the trigger's input naming Kai's application id and #general, and no AccessToken
    - the next run puts facts into the space's memory and writes Topics to the space
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: A server the space was not granted
  given: Kai is in the DXOS server and another server; the space was granted the DXOS server only
  when: a crawl asks fetchMessages for a channel of the other server
  then:
    - the bot host refuses it and Discord is not called
    - the channel is marked errored in the CrawlState with the host's reason
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Another space names the bot
  given: Kai's bot host owned by space A
  when: a crawl in space B calls fetchMessages naming space A
  then:
    - compute-service refuses the call before it reaches the bot host
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: A person who does not manage the server
  given: Kai is in a server where the signed-in person is a member without Manage Server
  when: they ask to index it
  then:
    - EDGE refuses the grant and the server's channels are not listed
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Stop indexing
  given: a back-index with one channel
  when: the person toggles Index off on that channel
  then:
    - the trigger is disabled, with no channels
    - the CrawlState is kept
```

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: Index the DXOS server, query its memory, and have the agent report on it
  desc: End to end on local Composer and EDGE — from a space holding only its Discord connection, the person indexes DXOS channels, the crawl runs on EDGE, the facts are queried in Brain's Memory view, and the agent turns them into sheets with charts, a deck and a summary.
  actors: human, agent
  status: unverified
  given:
    - a space whose only Discord data is the Discord sign-in connection and its token, with the space memory cleared
    - Kai installed in the DXOS server, and the space granted it (DXOS shows as indexed)
    - the Discord, Brain, Sheet, Presenter and Markdown plugins enabled, with a live model
  steps:
    - name: Pick the channels
      do: On the Discord connection's page, select DXOS and turn on general, announcements, sdk, composer, help and interesting.
      expect: each channel shows as indexed, and the back-index settings appear with "Not run yet."
    - name: Crawl back a year
      do: Set Crawl back to 365 days.
      expect: the trigger's input carries a 365-day window
    - name: Run the crawl on EDGE
      do: Click Check now and wait for the runs to finish.
      expect: the trace shows "Crawl Discord channels" running on EDGE, and the totals line counts the messages read
    - name: Query the memory
      do: Open Brain's Memory view and run a SPARQL query over the facts.
      expect: the statement count is above the seed vocabulary, and the query returns rows from the crawl
    - name: Ask for findings
      do: In a new chat, ask the agent to find the five most interesting things in its memory of the DXOS server and build a sheet with a chart for each, a deck of the charts and a markdown summary.
      expect: the agent queries the memory, then creates five sheets with charts, a presentation and a document
    - name: Open the deck and a finding
      do: Open the presentation, then one of the sheets.
      expect: a cover slide and one slide per chart; the sheet holds the rows the agent queried, with its chart
  note: What the findings are, and their titles and charts, are the model's, so they differ from take to take.
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: The plugin's back-index runs pipeline-discord's DiscordPipeline with the same stages as the CLI, with different dependencies injected. Its crawl state is an ECHO object, and it will eventually write into the space's memory service.
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The Pipeline panel takes the back-index's state from its ECHO objects.
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-6]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Extraction is set up the way agents are: install Composer's Discord bot (Kai) in the server from the Discord companion. The crawl and ConfigureBackIndex take the bot's application id and, for a bot that is not Kai, its access token, as BindChannel does, in place of a Connection. The crawl reads Discord through discord-service, which adds Kai's token. The companion gets a per-channel choice to index that calls ConfigureBackIndex.
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1, F-3, F-4, BackIndexInput, ConfigureBackIndex, CrawlDiscordChannels]
  why: A space then holds no token for Kai, and indexing is one more choice next to connecting a channel to the agent.
  rejected: A bot token pasted into a Connection, which puts a bot token in every space that indexes.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: Approve [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: user:dmaretskyi
```

```mdl
decision D-5: Kai's token is not exposed to operations; discord-service exposes a semantic source for the pipeline rather than a passthrough of Discord API requests.
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3, F-4, DiscordBotService]
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The source is two calls, listChannels and fetchMessages, answering Discord's message fields trimmed to what the crawl maps, and scoped to the servers in which the space has connected a channel. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.1, F-3.2, F-3.3, F-4.3, DiscordMessage, DiscordSourceChannel]
  why: These are the only two Discord reads the crawler's Source makes. Scoping by connected servers stops an owning space from reading every server the shared Kai app is in.
  rejected: A GET-only passthrough checked against the space, which lets the owning space read any guild, member list or user Kai can see.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: compute-service refuses a source call whose bot names a space other than the invocation's. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.5]
  why: The space in the call is the caller's to write; without the check a bundle in one space reads as another space's bot.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: A refused source call marks the channel as errored with the host's reason, and removing the last indexed channel disables the trigger rather than deleting the back-index. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1.3, F-5.2]
  why: The crawler isolates a failed target so the others continue; keeping the CrawlState lets re-indexing resume from its cursors.
```

```mdl
question Q-1: Kai's bot host serves one owner space per EDGE environment. How do other spaces index through Kai?
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.4, F-1.4]
  options:
    - Owner only: one space per environment indexes through Kai; others bring their own bot and token.
    - Per-guild owners: the bot host keys ownership by server, so each server belongs to the space that connected it.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: The crawl's only Discord dependency is DiscordService, and it depends on MemoryService: it writes facts with MemoryService.put instead of to a fact feed.
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.2, F-2.3, F-3.1, DiscordService, CrawlDiscordChannels, ConfigureBackIndex, BackIndexInput]
```

```mdl
decision D-10: DiscordService is a service of its own carrying only listChannels and fetchMessages, apart from the bot's act and findMembers; the back-index keeps no fact feed, so ConfigureBackIndex creates only the trigger and CrawlState. Fills in [D-9].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [DiscordService, F-1.3, F-6.1, ConfigureBackIndex]
  why: A crawl that can only read channels and messages cannot post or message people even through a bug; a feed nobody reads would only duplicate the memory.
  rejected: Adding the source calls to DiscordBotService, which hands the crawl the bot's write calls too.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: The crawl runs as plugin-discord's bundle under compute-service's worker loader, which gains invocation-scope keys for DiscordService and MemoryService, each pinned to the invocation's space. Fills in [D-9].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-7.1, F-7.2]
  why: plugin-discord is routed to bundles, not held on operation-service, and a bundle gets a service only by its key in the invocation scope, which offers no MemoryService today.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: The back-index names only the bot's application id, with no access token, and DiscordMessage keeps Discord's own field names (`referenced_message`, `message_reference`). Fills in [D-9].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [BackIndexInput, ConfigureBackIndex, DiscordMessage, F-4.2]
  why: The bot host already signs with the token its owner space bound it with, so a token reference in the trigger would go unused; Discord's field names let the plugin map a message the same way whether it came from the REST API or the bot host.
  rejected: Carrying the access token id in every read, which the host would only compare with the one it holds.
```

```mdl
decision D-13: The back-index is the space's extraction pipeline: the memory service is the space's, and setting it up needs no agent.
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1, F-3.2, F-3.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-14: A space reads a server under an index grant held on the bot host apart from agent bindings, given only to a person who owns the server or holds Manage Server there, checked against their own Discord sign-in. Reads use the bot's token without the owner or a running gateway. Fills in [D-13].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-3.2, F-3.4, F-8]
  why: Holding the read right apart from bindings leaves agent routing untouched and lets several spaces index through the one shared Kai app; checking Manage Server stops a space member from granting their space a server that is not theirs.
  rejected: Claiming the bot's owner by indexing, which ties extraction to routing and lets only one space index through Kai; a grant per channel, which adds a row and a check for every channel.
```

```mdl
decision D-15: Setup lives in a Discord section of space settings, applies each channel toggle at once, and indexes no channel until it is picked. The agent companion keeps routing only. Fills in [D-13].
  date: 2026-11-18
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-1]
  why: The back-index is the space's, so its setup sits with the space; one place to index keeps the agent companion about routing.
  rejected: A deck companion beside Memory and Pipeline; a batched Apply button; every public channel picked by default.
```

